  "verdict_rule": "The fixed tree builds and passes with the reference unit, so a failure after only the candidate is integrated is FAIL: a rejected class, compile or elaboration error at any file, simulator failure or missing test output. Only an integrated source that differs from the submission, a failed fixed-input check, a missing tool, resource exhaustion and a wall-clock interruption are INVALID.",
  "simulation_limit": {
    "option": "+max-cycles=2500000",
    "wall_clock_seconds": 3600,
    "rule": "A program that reaches the cycle limit, ends without its PASSED or FAILED line, or exits the simulator abnormally is FAIL_INCOMPLETE_EXECUTION. The longest program with the reference CPU, rv64mi-p-cache_replacement_cycles, ends after 202,604 cycles. A wall-clock interruption or a resource or tool failure is INVALID unless the trace already differs from Spike."
